{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>It overwhelms him like a king</b> — that he is ready to enter into battle and has no equal. And some say: that troubles surround him like the encircling of the sphere around the globe, which is the earth, and it would be like כדור אל ארץ, and the kaf of כדור drops, and the kaf of כידור is a root-letter, and it is far-fetched."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase כדור אל ארץ is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The argument turns on whether the kaf in כדור is separable (a prefixed particle that 'drops') or inseparable (a root letter in כידור), the latter possibility which he dismisses as רחוק (far-fetched)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:44.229335312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}